<title>PORTUGAL: Yield edges higher on Portugal 5-yr bonds.</title>
<headline>Yield edges higher on Portugal 5-yr bonds.</headline>
<dateline>LISBON 1997-01-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following is the result of the Institute for Public Credit Management's (IGCP) auction of 25 billion escudos of five-year, fixed-rate bonds (OT).</p>
<p>ISSUER: Republic of Portugal   MATURITY:23/3/2002</p>
<p>COUPON:5.75	  AVERAGE ACCEPTED YIELD:5.716272</p>
<p>HIGHEST ACCEPTED YIELD: 5.77 LOWEST ACCEPTED: 5.58</p>
<p>AMOUNT PLACED: 24.92 billion  AMOUNT BID:79.67</p>
<p>PAYMENT FREQUENCY:Annual</p>
<p>NOTES: The issue is fungible. The auction takes to 61.79 billion the total amount of the bonds issued.</p>
</text>
